  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Clear family service wayfinding",
    "overview": "The parent may be reading a phone in ordinary daylight while managing household demands. Light, flat surfaces and readable sans-serif type support quick scanning. Dark navy carries structure; teal identifies actions and selections; soft lemon highlights support and necessary choices. Color never supplies the only state cue.\n\nPublic pages explain the service, offer food or utility entry, and expose urgent official help. The application prioritizes the family's task. No generic chat console or analytics dashboard sits between the need and useful action.\n\nUse one primary action per task, progressive detail, clear labels and visible focus. The three intake stages preserve answers and retry identity. Required parent actions precede operator-owned waiting, which stays secondary. Show sources and detailed permission without forcing repetitive approval.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One clear task at a time",
      "Parent action before service waiting",
      "Honest recorded outcomes"
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve one clear action, source attribution and honest progress.",
      "Do keep operator-owned waiting quieter than the family's necessary step."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Do not introduce an agent transcript, analytics dashboard or fabricated receipt into the family journey."
    ]
  }
